{{also|Middle-earth|middle earth|Middle Earth}}
==English==

===Alternative forms===
* [[middle earth]], [[Middle Earth]]

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|enm}} {{term|myddyl erthe|lang=enm}}, alteration (as if {{term|middel||middle|lang=enm}} + {{term|erthe||earth|lang=enm}}) of earlier {{term|middelerd|lang=enm}}, {{term|middenerd||middle-earth|lang=enm}}, from {{etyl|ang}} {{term|middangeard|middanġeard|the globe, world, earth, mankind|lit=middle yard, middle inclosure, middle region|lang=ang}} (compare {{term|mid}}, {{term|yard}}), though often interpreted since Old English times as {{term|||middle + earth}}. Cognate with {{etyl|is|-}} {{term|miðgarðr||Midgard|lang=is}}, {{etyl|got|-}} {{term|||tr=midjungards|mid-yard, middle abode|lang=got}}. See {{l|en|Midgard}}.

===Noun===
{{en-noun|sg=[[middle]]-[[earth]]|-}}

# {{archaic}} The physical world, as imagined between [[heaven]] and [[hell]], or pre-Christian equivalents.

